# Ownership points at @leeknowsai, a single verified org member, because
# @TracyHQ/registry-maintainers does not exist yet. Switch to the team once it
# does — one person is a single point of failure for review.
#
# This file only gates merges because branch protection on `main` has "Require
# review from Code Owners" turned on. It was turned on the day the repo was
# created, before the first record could be submitted. Without that rule this
# file is advisory, and the sibling MCP registry shipped in exactly that state
# for a while; the consequence there was small because a submission could not
# reach a measured field. Here it can.

# registry/ IS OWNED HERE, AND THAT IS THE DIFFERENCE FROM THE MCP REGISTRY.
#
# There, registry/ is deliberately unowned: platform namespaces are reserved, so
# a submission physically cannot touch a measurement and anyone may merge one.
# Here every record lives under a platform namespace and submissions write into
# the same record the crawler wrote. `src/validate.ts` refuses the measured
# fields, but the rest of the record still needs a human to look at it.
#
# "Anyone can submit" is still true: opening a pull request needs no permission.
# Merging one needs a reader.
/registry/   @leeknowsai

/curation/   @leeknowsai
/data/       @leeknowsai
/schema/     @leeknowsai
/src/        @leeknowsai
/bin/        @leeknowsai
/scripts/    @leeknowsai
/.github/    @leeknowsai
